These are real improvements, not commit-message optimism.

Full SHA-256 is now actually full SHA-256 rather than 16 hexadecimal characters.

`WorkerKit.close()` now commits the actual chain head plus event count rather than literally writing `"ok"`.

The SDK now explicitly denies an irreversible action when `VerificationResult.status != PASS`. That fixes one of the nastiest bugs from the previous version.

