# One important strategic correction: don't say “built on ERC-8004 / 8183 / 7710” yet

They're excellent targets.

But **all three are currently Draft ERCs**.

ERC-8004 is explicitly Draft and defines identity, reputation and validation registries for agent trust. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][1])

ERC-8183 is also Draft. Its model is particularly relevant to Moltwork because it explicitly defines an agent-commerce job lifecycle around `Open → Funded → Submitted → Completed/Rejected/Expired` with a separate evaluator. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][2])

ERC-7710 is likewise Draft and standardizes delegated capabilities, including bounded permissions for automated/AI systems. ([Ethereum Improvement Proposals][3])

So the architecture should say:

> **compatible with / integrating emerging ERC-8004, ERC-8183 and ERC-7710**

rather than making them foundational dependencies.

This actually reinforces your chain-agnostic thesis.

Your canonical schema should survive if any of those drafts change.

